Ninaro - HELP - Ninaro - HELP - Ninaro - HELP - Ninaro -

~How To Use Help
Press ESC or F1 to exit help. If you used the menu to get
help, the keys you used in the menu work here. Otherwise
you used F1 or H to get help, and the arrow keys work here.
Please ensure that NumLock is off (by pressing the NumLock
key on the numerical keypad to the right of your keyboard
until the NumLock light is off). The table below shows what
these keys do.

~Table of Help Keys
Key         Function
Left        Scrolls UP a page
Right       Scrolls DOWN a page
Up          Scrolls UP a line
Down        Scrolls DOWN a line
PageUp      Scrolls UP a page
PageDown    Scrolls DOWN a page
Home        Scrolls to the top of help
End         Scrolls to the end of help

~Ninaro
Ninaro stands for N-in-a-row, which means that the connect
four game has been extended to connect any number on any
sized grid. Logically however a minimum of 3x3x3 applies.

~How To Play
The aim of the game is to connect a number of tokens in the
grid while stopping your opponent from doing so. The first
player to make the connection wins. The number of tokens you
must connect to win is shown at the top right of the screen,
under the Connect heading. Connections can take in four
different ways. These are vertical, horizontal, slope 1 (/)
or slope 2 (\).

~Player's Keys
Each player has a set of keys, consisting of Left,Right,Up,
Down,Select and Cancel. The table below shows these keys.

~Table of Player Keys
        Player One      Player Two
Left        A           Keypad 4
Right       D           Keypad 6
Up          W           Keypad 8
Down        S           Keypad 2
Select      E           Enter
Cancel      Q           Backspace

The keypad keys can be used as either the grey arrow keys
or the numbered keys on the numerical keypad for which
numlock must be off.

~What The Keys Do.
Depending on where you are in the program, the keys do
different things, though they are quite similar. The
table below shows the functionality of the keys at each
location on the program.

~Table of Key Functionality
        Playing A Game      Using Menu      Using Dialogs
Left    Token Left          Left a Menu     Left an item
Right   Token Right         Right a Menu    Right an item
Up      Calls the menu      Up an item      Up a group
Down    Drops Token         Down an item    Down a group
Select  Drops Token         Select item     Select Button-
                                            OK,Reset,Cancel
Cancel  Calls the menu      Cancel Menu     Cancels Dialog

~The Mouse
Only Player One has access to the mouse, left-click acts as
Select while right-click acts as Cancel. Apart from a few
minor differences, moving the mouse acts as moving keys.
The differences are as follows : Moving the mouse in itself
does nothing. Only Selecting while on a spot does anything.
To enter a token move the mouse to the appropriate column
in the grid and press Select (left-click). Obviously using
the right mouse button as Cancel calls the menu.

~The Menus.
The menus are the key way in Ninaro of changing things. The
menu is accessable at almost anytime by pressing ESC, M for
menu, or your appropriate player key.

~The Game Menu
The game menu lets you control the game.
New     - starts a new game
Load    - loads the saved game
Save    - saves the game
End     - ends the current game, when no game is on all
          options are accessable (e.g. player one and two)
          dialogs.
Suggest - suggests a move to make. The move is suggested by
Move      AI Genius.
Toggle  - toggles the sound On and Off
Sound
Exit    - exits the game

~The Board Menu
The board menu lets you change the board attributes
7x8x4   - changes the board to 7 Columns, 8 Rows,Connect 4
12x13x6 - changes the board to 12 Columns,13 Rows,Connect 4
Custom  - changes the board via The Custom Board Dialog

~The Player Menu
The player menu lets you change the player attributes
One...  - changes the attributes of player one via The
          Player Dialog
Two...  - changes the attributes of player two via The
          Player Dialog
Options - changes the player options via The Player Options
          Dialog
Reset   - resets both player's scores to zero.
Scores

~The Help Menu
The help menu provides all your help needs, via this screen.
Help is available at anytime by pressing either F1 or H.

~The Dialogs
Dialogs help you choose from a group of options. In the
dialogs C cancels, R resets and O ok's. Pressing Select
at any time while in the dialog results on the hilited
button (OK,Reset,Cancel) being used, while pressing cancel
cancels the dialog.

